-- title:
--   Lemma 6.1 — absolute continuity of MDP values
-- statement:
--   For $p\in\{1,2\}$, let $P$ and $\tilde P$ be player-$p$ MDPs with identical state and action sets and discount factor $\lambda\in[0,1)$, transition functions $\delta,\tilde\delta$, and reward functions $r,\tilde r$ (values in $[0,1]$). Let
--   $$\eta=\max_{s\in S,a\in A}\max\Big\{|r(s,a)-\tilde r(s,a)|,\ \sum_{s'\in S}|\delta(s,a)(s')-\tilde\delta(s,a)(s')|\Big\}.$$
--   Then $|\mathrm{val}^P_\lambda(s)-\mathrm{val}^{\tilde P}_\lambda(s)|\le\eta/(1-\lambda)$ for all states $s$.
--
--   This bounds the effect of removing small probabilities from a strategy.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite game G = (S, A, B, δ) with |S| = n and at most m actions per player → states Fin n, actions Fin mA and Fin mB with n, mA, mB ≥ 1, m = max(mA, mB), distributions as nonnegative real vectors summing to one; reason: relabelling of finite sets; nonempty state and action sets are the source game convention
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
--   - encoding: a player-p MDP P = (S, A, δ) for p ∈ {1, 2} → a game with the other player's action set Fin 1 (CSG n m 1 for p = 1, CSG n 1 m for p = 2); the theorem is the conjunction of the two cases; reason: the source defines a player-p MDP as the special CSG where the other player has one action
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 6.1, printed p. 18 (PDF p. 20)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 6.1 (Continuity).** For player-`p` MDPs `P, P̃` (`p ∈ {1,2}`) with identical state and
action sets and discount factor `λ`, transition functions `δ, δ̃` and rewards `r, r̃`, let
`η = max_{s,a} max(|r(s,a) - r̃(s,a)|, ∑_{s'} |δ(s,a)(s') - δ̃(s,a)(s')|)`. Then
`|val^P_λ(s) - val^{P̃}_λ(s)| ≤ η / (1 - λ)` for every state `s`. -/
theorem lemma_6_1 :
    (∀ {n m : ℕ} (P P' : CSG n m 1) (r r' : Reward n m 1), IsReward r → IsReward r' →
      ∀ lam : ℝ, 0 ≤ lam → lam < 1 →
        ∀ s, |discValue P r lam s - discValue P' r' lam s| ≤
          (⨆ s₀ : Fin n, ⨆ a : Fin m, max |r s₀ a 0 - r' s₀ a 0|
            (∑ s', |(P.δ s₀ a 0).1 s' - (P'.δ s₀ a 0).1 s'|)) / (1 - lam)) ∧
    (∀ {n m : ℕ} (P P' : CSG n 1 m) (r r' : Reward n 1 m), IsReward r → IsReward r' →
      ∀ lam : ℝ, 0 ≤ lam → lam < 1 →
        ∀ s, |discValue P r lam s - discValue P' r' lam s| ≤
          (⨆ s₀ : Fin n, ⨆ b : Fin m, max |r s₀ 0 b - r' s₀ 0 b|
            (∑ s', |(P.δ s₀ 0 b).1 s' - (P'.δ s₀ 0 b).1 s'|)) / (1 - lam)) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
